# REGRESSION — `MatchItem::MetaFor` carries an `arm_template` whose body
# IS emitted by the meta expansion, and these walkers run on the
# UNEXPANDED AST. An `if let MatchItem::Arm(..)` with no else walked it
# blind -- a catch-all in a second syntactic costume, inside functions a
# catch-all lint already pinned.
#
# The liveness walker is UNDER-APPROXIMATION-CRITICAL: a use it cannot see
# makes a variable look dead at an earlier consuming position, so the value is
# MOVED instead of cloned and the later read finds freed memory. Every cell
# below was rc 0 printing GARBAGE on BOTH backends at the commit named, with
# ggdef printing the right answer wherever it can adjudicate.
#
# Found by R45 Track D brief-review pass 15; RED-verified by the orchestrator
# against the pre-fix compiler.
#
# ⚠ The `v.set(0, ...)` is load-bearing: it frees the value moved into the
# vector. Without it the moved-from read still finds live memory and prints
# correctly — a fixture that proves nothing.
# PROBE C — a runtime local used ONLY inside a `meta for` match-arm template.
# `walk_stmt`'s `Stmt::Match` arm does `if let MatchItem::Arm(arm) = item`, so
# `MatchItem::MetaFor` arms are SKIPPED. Liveness runs on the UNEXPANDED AST
# (functions.rs:1429) and the arm expansion happens later
# (functions.rs:~1473),
# so the use inside the template is invisible.
#
# The `v.set(0, ...)` is load-bearing: it frees the value moved into the
# vector.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

enum Shape:
    Circle(int)
    Square(int)

int f(Shape sh):
    String s = mk("abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789", "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ")
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(s)
    v.set(0, mk("xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx", "yyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyyy"))
    match sh:
        meta for vname, T in variant_payloads(Shape):
            case vname(x):
                print(s)
                return x
    return 0

void main():
    print(f(Shape.Circle(7)))
